t explicitly NEED NOT meet RECIST 1.1 criteria for unequivocal progression, so the 5 mm bar does not apply here.","v":["no","yes"]},{"d":"irecist-nl-inc","k":"enum","l":"New lesions: sum of measures of new lesion-target up by at least 5 mm, OR any increase in new lesion-non-target, OR additional new lesions, since the prior iUPD.","v":["no","yes"]},{"d":"irecist-newcat","k":"enum","l":"Whether RECIST 1.1 defined progression is now present in a lesion category that had NOT previously met progression criteria. This also confirms iCPD.","v":["no","yes"]}],"ireton-jones":[{"d":"ij-mode","k":"enum","l":"Ventilation status","v":["ventilated","spontaneous"]},{"d":"ij-age","k":"number","l":"Age","u":"yr","r":1},{"d":"ij-wt","k":"number","l":"Weight","u":"kg","r":1},{"d":"ij-ht","k":"number","l":"Height (spontaneous form, for BMI)","u":"cm"},{"d":"ij-sex","k":"enum","l":"Sex (male indicator, ventilated form)","v":["male","female"]},{"d":"ij-trauma","k":"bool","l":"Trauma (ventilated form modifier)"},{"d":"ij-burn","k":"bool","l":"Burn (ventilated form modifier)"}],"iron-ganzoni":[{"d":"w","k":"number","l":"Weight","u":"kg","r":1},{"d":"hb","k":"number","l":"Current Hb","u":"g/dL","r":1},{"d":"tgt","k":"number","l":"Target Hb","u":"g/dL","r":1},{"d":"stores","k":"number","l":"Iron stores override","u":"mg"}],"isaric-4c-mortality":[{"d":"is4c-age","k":"number","l":"Age (years)"},{"d":"is4c-sex","k":"enum","l":"Sex","v":["female","male"]},{"d":"is4c-com","k":"number","l":"Number of comorbidities"},{"d":"is4c-rr","k":"number","l":"Respiratory rate (/min)"},{"d":"is4c-spo2","k":"number","l":"SpO2 on room air (%)"},{"d":"is4c-gcs","k":"number","l":"Glasgow Coma Scale"},{"d":"is4c-urea","k":"number","l":"Urea"},{"d":"is4c-ureaunit","k":"enum","l":"Urea unit","v":["mmol","bun-mgdl"]},{"d":"is4c-crp","k":"number","l":"CRP (mg/L)"}],"isg-1990-behcet":[{"d":"isg-oral","k":"bool","l":"Recurrent oral ulceration"},{"d":"isg-gen","k":"bool","l":"Recurrent genital ulceration"},{"d":"isg-eye","k":"bool","l":"Eye lesions (uveitis / retinal vasculitis)"},{"d":"isg-skin","k":"bool","l":"Skin lesions"},{"d":"isg-path","k":"bool","l":"Positive pathergy test"}],"isgls-bile-leak":[{"d":"bile-gate","k":"bool","l":"Drain bilirubin >= 3x serum on/after POD 3, OR need for radiologic/operative intervention (the bile-leak gate)","r":1},{"d":"bile-c","k":"bool","l":"Requires relaparotomy (Grade C)"},{"d":"bile-b","k":"bool","l":"Change in management without relaparotomy (percutaneous drainage, ERCP/stent), or a grade A leak persisting > 1 week (Grade B)"}],"isgls-phlf":[{"d":"phlf-gate","k":"bool","l":"Increased INR (or FFP need) AND hyperbilirubinemia on/after POD 5 (rising if abnormal preop) — the PHLF gate","r":1},{"d":"phlf-c","k":"bool","l":"Requires invasive treatment: hemodialysis/RRT, mechanical ventilation, vasopressors, rescue hepatectomy or salvage transplant (Grade C)"},{"d":"phlf-b","k":"bool","l":"Deviation managed without invasive treatment: FFP, albumin, diuretics, non-invasive ventilation, or ICU admission alone (Grade B)"}],"isgps-dge":[{"d":"dge-ngt","k":"number","l":"Nasogastric tube required (days): 4-7 = A, 8-14 = B, >14 = C"},{"d":"dge-reinsert","k":"number","l":"NGT reinsertion postoperative day (0 = none): after POD 3 = A, after POD 7 = B, after POD 14 = C"},{"d":"dge-solids","k":"number","l":"Unable to tolerate solid oral intake by postoperative day (0 = tolerating): POD 7 = A, POD 14 = B, POD 21 = C"}],"isgps-popf":[{"d":"popf-gate","k":"bool","l":"Drain amylase > 3x upper limit of normal serum amylase, on/after POD 3 (the POPF gate)","r":1},{"d":"popf-c","k":"bool","l":"Reoperation, single/multiple organ failure, or death attributable to POPF (Grade C)"},{"d":"popf-b","k":"bool","l":"Clinically relevant change in management: drains > 3 wk or repositioned, percutaneous/endoscopic drainage, octreotide/antibiotics, angio for bleeding, or infection without organ failure (Grade B)"}],"ishlt-rejection":[{"d":"ishlt-grade","k":"enum","l":"The revised ISHLT grade. Enter the R form only - a 1990-scheme grade or a bare number is refused with its mapping, because the two schemes reuse the same numbers [0R = Grade 0R (no rejection): No evidence of rejection: unremarkable endomyocardium with no lymphocytic infiltration. (from 1990 grade 0) 1R = Grade 1R (mild, low grade): Interstitial and/or perivascular infiltrate with up to one focus of myocyte damage. Myocardial architecture is otherwise intact. (from 1990 grades 1A, 1B, 2) 2R = Grade 2R (moderate, intermediate grade): Two or more foci of infiltrate with associated myocyte damage, with uninvolved myocardium present between the foci. (from 1990 grade 3A) 3R = Grade 3R (severe, high grade): Diffuse infiltrate with multifocal myocyte damage, with or without edema, hemorrhage, or vasculitis. A diffuse process in which distinct foci cannot be made out. (from 1990 grades 3B, 4)]","r":1,"v":["0R","1R","2R","3R"]}],"ishoo-angioedema":[{"d":"ish-faceorlip","k":"bool","l":"Face or lip swelling (stage I)"},{"d":"ish-softpalate","k":"bool","l":"Soft palate swelling (stage II)"},{"d":"ish-tongue","k":"bool","l":"Tongue swelling (stage III)"},{"d":"ish-larynx","k":"bool","l":"Laryngeal swelling (stage IV)"},{"d":"ish-airwaythreatened","k":"bool","l":"The airway is threatened right now (an emergency at any stage; it overrides the staging)"}],"isi":[{"d":"isi-fall","k":"enum","l":"Difficulty falling asleep (0-4)","r":1,"v":["0","1","2","3","4"]},{"d":"isi-stay","k":"enum","l":"Difficulty staying asleep (0-4)","r":1,"v":["0","1","2","3","4"]},{"d":"isi-early","k":"enum","l":"Waking up too early (0-4)","r":1,"v":["0","1","2","3","4"]},{"d":"isi-dissat","k":"enum","l":"Dissatisfaction with sleep pattern (0-4)","r":1,"v":["0","1","2","3","4"]},{"d":"isi-notice","k":"enum","l":"How noticeable to others (0-4)","r":1,"v":["0","1","2","3","4"]},{"d":"isi-worry","k":"enum","l":"Worry / distress about sleep (0-4)","r":1,"v":["0","1","2","3","4"]},{"d":"isi-interfere","k":"enum","l":"Interference with daily functioning (0-4)","r":1,"v":["0","1","2","3","4"]}],"isis-shoulder":[{"d":"isis-age","k":"bool","l":"Age ≤20 years at surgery"},{"d":"isis-comp","k":"bool","l":"Competitive sport participation"},{"d":"isis-contact","k":"bool","l":"Contact or forced-overhead sport"},{"d":"isis-lax","k":"bool","l":"Shoulder hyperlaxity (anterior or inferior)"},{"d":"isis-hs","k":"bool","l":"Hill-Sachs on AP external-rotation radiograph"},{"d":"isis-glenoid","k":"bool","l":"Glenoid loss of contour on AP radiograph"}],"isl-lymphedema":[{"d":"isl-stage","k":"enum","l":"The stage, describing what the tissue has become [0 = Stage 0 (latent or subclinical): Swelling is not yet evident despite impaired lymph transport, with subtle alterations in tissue fluid and composition and changes in subjective symptoms. Not applicable. Not applicable: there is no overt edema to pit. I = Stage I: An early accumulation of fluid relatively high in protein content. The swelling SUBSIDES with limb elevation. Pitting MAY occur. II = Stage II: More changes in solid structures. Limb elevation alone RARELY reduces the tissue swelling. Pitting IS manifest. late II = Late stage II: Excess subcutaneous fat and fibrosis develop. Elevation does not reduce the swelling. The limb MAY NOT pit. That is fibrosis replacing fluid, not improvement. III = Stage III: Lymphostatic elephantiasis, with trophic skin changes such as acanthosis, alterations in skin character and thickness, further deposition of fat and fibrosis, and warty overgrowths. Elevation does not reduce the swelling. Pitting CAN BE ABSENT. Again, that is fibrosis, not improvement.]","r":1,"v":["0","I","II","late II","III"]},{"d":"isl-severity","k":"enum","l":"Severity by excess volume difference between limbs - a SEPARATE axis from the stage [none = Not graded, Excess volume at or below 5 percent. Subclinical lymphedema is measurable from about 3 to 5 percent, which sits below the minimal grade, so a limb can be measurably abnormal and still ungraded. minimal = Minimal, Excess volume above 5 percent and below 20 percent. moderate = Moderate, Excess volume of 20 to 40 percent. severe = Severe, Excess volume above 40 percent.]","r":1,"v":["none","minimal","moderate","severe"]},{"d":"isl-bilateral","k":"enum","l":"Is the swelling bilateral? Required, because the severity grade is an inter-limb comparison and bilateral swelling understates the disease.","r":1,"v":["no","yes"]}],"iss-rts":[{"d":"ir-ais1","k":"number","l":"Highest AIS region (0-6)","r":1},{"d":"ir-ais2","k":"number","l":"2nd highest AIS region (0-6)","r":1},{"d":"ir-ais3","k":"number","l":"3rd highest AIS region (0-6)","r":1},{"d":"ir-gcs","k":"number","l":"Glasgow Coma Scale (3-15)","r":1},{"d":"ir-sbp","k":"number","l":"Systolic BP","u":"mmHg","r":1},{"d":"ir-rr","k":"number","l":"Respiratory rate","u":"/min","r":1}],"isth-bat":[{"d":"isth-group","k":"enum","l":"Patient group (sets the abnormal threshold)","r":1,"v":["male","female","child"]},{"d":"isth-epistaxis","k":"number","l":"Epistaxis (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-cutaneous","k":"number","l":"Cutaneous / bruising (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-minorWounds","k":"number","l":"Bleeding from minor wounds (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-oralCavity","k":"number","l":"Oral cavity (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-gi","k":"number","l":"GI bleeding (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-hematuria","k":"number","l":"Hematuria (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-toothExtraction","k":"number","l":"Tooth extraction (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-surgery","k":"number","l":"Surgery (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-menorrhagia","k":"number","l":"Menorrhagia (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-postpartum","k":"number","l":"Postpartum hemorrhage (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-muscleHematoma","k":"number","l":"Muscle hematoma (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-hemarthrosis","k":"number","l":"Hemarthrosis (0–4)"},{"d":"isth-cns","k":"number","l":"CNS bleeding (0, 3, or 4)"},{"d":"isth-other","k":"number","l":"Other bleeding (0–4)"}],"isth-dic":[{"d":"id-gate","k":"bool","l":"Underlying disorder associated with DIC is present (required gate)"},{"d":"id-plt","k":"enum","l":"Platelet count (>100 = 0, 50-100 = 1, <50 = 2)","r":1,"v":[">100","50-100","<50"]},{"d":"id-fdp","k":"enum","l":"Fibrin marker (none = 0, moderate = 2, strong = 3)","r":1,"v":["none","moderate","strong"]},{"d":"id-pt","k":"enum","l":"Prolonged PT (<3s = 0, 3-6s = 1, >6s = 2)","r":1,"v":["<3s","3-6s",">6s"]},{"d":"id-fib","k":"enum","l":"Fibrinogen (>1 = 0, <=1 = 1)","r":1,"v":[">1","<=1"]}],"iv-osmolarity":[{"d":"io-dex","k":"number","l":"Dextrose","u":"%","r":1},{"d":"io-aa","k":"number","l":"Amino acids","u":"%","r":1},{"d":"io-na","k":"number","l":"Sodium additives","u":"mEq/L","r":1},{"d":"io-k","k":"number","l":"Potassium additives","u":"mEq/L","r":1}],"ivc-fluid-responsiveness":[{"d":"iv-mode","k":"enum","l":"Ventilation mode","r":1,"v":["mechanical","spontaneous"]},{"d":"iv-dmax","k":"number","l":"Maximum IVC diameter","u":"cm","r":1},{"d":"iv-dmin","k":"number","l":"Minimum IVC diameter","u":"cm","r":1}]}